Anecdote: I first heard of (or became interested in) Lojban (as opposed to =
Loglan) is a message posted to Conlang by John in which he translated=20
something or other (some kind of Prolog program, I seem to recall) into=20
Lojban. And incredible as it may seem (& it certainly does to me), I was=20
entranced by its rhythmic and segmental euphony. All I can remember now=20
is that the rhythm was dactyllic/anapestic and that it contained the word=20
"jonja'e".

Nowadays I find Lojban so excruciatingly ugly that it genuinely causes me
palpable pain to read or write it.

